      "id": 487949,
      "username": "Hemil_Sangani",
      "name": "Hemil Sangani",
      "created_at": "2025-12-02T10:29:19.496Z",
      "cooked": "<ul>\n<li>The prefix list in <strong>Document Naming Settings</strong> only displays naming prefixes that are configured or predefined globally.</li>\n<li>Custom prefixes set within a DocType or naming rule are local to that DocType and hence not synced to the global prefix list.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you want a specific starting number for the suffix, you can configure the <strong>Counter</strong> field in the Document Naming Rule.<br>\nFor example, if you set the counter to <strong>100</strong>, the next generated document will begin from <strong>101</strong>.</p>",
